	(text "U5 priority mode: VIN1 = USB_5V (eFuse fallback), VIN2 = BATT_SYS (charger OUT or battery).\nR40/R41 set the switch point: 1.0 V x (300k+100k)/100k = 4.0 V, 3.68-4.32 V with VREF tolerance.\nWith USB present the system runs from U3 and does not depend on the charger.\nSwitching is break-before-make (8 us at 5 V); the new channel waits until VSYS falls to its input.\nC40, C41 hold VSYS through that time. Regulator stays in range because input stays above 1.8 V.\nU6 TPS63001: 1.8-5.5 V in, 3.3 V out, 1200 mA in buck, up to 800 mA in boost, TI SLVS520C.\nSW3 pulls U6 EN low to turn the device off. All loads run from 3V3, so they all switch off.\nCharging continues with SW3 off. Battery still feeds U4 and U5 quiescent current, sense dividers.\nPS/SYNC default: power save enabled through R44. Fit R45 and remove R44 for forced PWM if audio needs it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d1bd9711-9337-5aba-b3b2-dbab7c21f613")
	)
)
